            <ArticleTitle>Endoscopic treatment for endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endometriosis is best regarded as a chronic disease that can vary in symptomatology over time. Endoscopic therapy for relief of pelvic pain as well as infertility is a therapeutic option. The formation of a rational treatment plan before surgery will ensure a minimum number of reproductive surgeries over the patient's lifetime.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
